-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",24,{
[737]="70069DF1\n1\tForage for wild carrots (total: 6)\tWild carrots grow on a hill to the south of Ivoreth's location in the Angle of Mitheithel. Collect wild carrots to join Ivoreth for a meal.\n2\tReturn to Ivoreth with the carrots you collected\tYou have collected wild carrots to share a meal with Ivoreth. You should return to her at her camp in the Angle of Mitheithel.\n",
[738]="70058356\n1\tRemove the rockslides from the path (total: 6)\tRockslides can be found on the path west of the Rushgate in Elderslade. You should remove the rockslides from the path for Foreman Brumbur.\n2\tSearch the hill for the source of the rockslides\tRockslides can be found on the path west of the Rushgate in Elderslade. You should search the hill for the source of the rockslides.\n3\tDefeat mountain stone-claws within Klórgren (total: 10)\030Defeat mountain deep-claws within Klórgren (total: 4)\tStone-claws and deep-claws can be found within the burrows of Klórgren in Elderslade. You should defeat some of the stone-claws and deep-claws within Klórgren.\n4\tCompleted\tPut a stop to the rockslides troubling the roads.\n",
[739]="70066CC8\n1\tDefeat Neekerbreekers in Springer's Close (total: 6)\030Defeat lynx in Loxhall (total: 6)\tLuingil has asked you to clear the road north of Neekerbreekers and lynx.\n2\tTalk to Luingil in Echad Lendir\tYou have cleared a path on the central road to Iáphel in Pinnath Gelin. You should report your progress to Luingil in Echad Lendir.\n",
[740]="70061444\n1\tTalk to Postmaster Proudfoot in Michel Delving\tPostmaster Proudfoot can be found outside the Quick Post in Michel Delving. Mayor Will Whitfoot has authorized Postmaster Proudfoot to alter the route to Nobottle. It now begins in Michel Delving, passes through Little Delving, and follows the road northward into Yondershire. You should inform Postmaster Proudfoot of the Mayor's decision.\n2\tCollect the satchels from Onyx Nethercot inside the Quick Post in Michel Delving\tOnyx Nethercot can be found inside the Quick Post in Michel Delving. Postmaster Proudfoot has asked you to collect the satchels for Yondershire from Onyx Nethercot inside the Quick Post in Michel Delving.\n3\tTalk to Onyx Nethercot in the Quick Post in Michel Delving\tOnyx Nethercot can be found inside the Quick Post in Michel Delving. Postmaster Proudfoot has asked you to collect the satchels for Yondershire from Onyx Nethercot inside the Quick Post in Michel Delving. You should talk to Onyx Nethercot.\n4\tCollect the satchel from Postmaster Proudfoot's table\tThe revised route to Nobottle begins in Michel Delving, continues into Little Delving, and follows the road northward into Yondershire. The satchel of mail for Yondershire can be found on Postmaster Proudfoot's table outside the Quick Post in Michel Delving. You should carry the satchel to Postman Grubb in Nobottle.\n5\tTalk to Postman Grubb in Nobottle\tPostman Grubb can be found outside the Quick Post in Nobottle, in Yondershire. You have successfully delivered the latest mail to Yondershire and outwitted the so-called \"Chief Shirriff\" in his efforts to seize control of the Quick Post. You should talk to Postman Grubb.\n",
[741]="70017578\n1\tTalk to Márus at the Shadowed Refuge\030Collect the rune-stone from Gaelnath\tGaelnath should be found in the Foundations of Stone, far to the east of Thorin's Hall. Dwalin told you to recover the dwarf-make rune-stone from the spider Gaelnath and bring it to Márus.\n",
[742]="70018199\n1\tDefeat Helegfan\tHelegfan can be found in the Sixteenth Hall, at the south-eastern tip of Nud-Melek, just north of the Foundations of Stone. Ríon has instructed you to aid your fellow rune-keepers with their final task upon the path to obtain a Rune of Restoration.\n2\tTalk to Ríon outside the Sixteenth Hall\tRíon is just outside of the Sixteenth Hall. You should return to Ríon and inform him of your success.\n",
[743]="7004CE2B\n1\tFind the captured raft-elf\tThe captured raft-elf is somewhere in Esgaroth-of-old. You should find the captured raft-elf.\n2\tDefeat Blengur\tBlengur can be found in Esgaroth-of-old. You should defeat Blengur.\n3\tTalk to the captured raft-elf\tThe captured raft-elf can be found in Esgaroth-of-old. You should talk to the captured raft-elf.\n4\tTalk to Mervárth\tMervárth is standing guard outside Esgaroth-of-old. You should talk to Mervárth.\n",
[744]="700413BC\n1\tSpeak with Arvaethor\tArvaethor can be found within the caverns of Nimrond. Arvaethor asks for you to follow him to the very heart of the caverns, deep inside the mountain.\n2\tSpeak with Arvaethor\tArvaethor can be found in the village of Ethring. You should speak with Arvaethor.\n",
[745]="70000D4F\n1\tPick up the sack of feed\tThe sack of feed can be found on the Grange north of Hobbiton. Once you have picked up the feed, bring them back to Belco in Tuckborough. Belco has told you that his pig, Old Sally, has a ravenous appetite, and that he needs more feed if he is to satisfy her. He has instructed you to go to the Grange and pick up a sack of feed.\n",
[746]="70000DD6\n1\tTalk to Gammer Boffin\tGammer Boffin is in Overhill, some considerable distance north of Tuckborough, on the other side of Hobbiton. Before you can collect new queen-bees for Farmer Proudfoot, you will need to obtain the means to protect yourself from the stings of the wild bees. Proudfoot told you to get a special balm from Gammer Boffin.\n2\tBring the toad-stones to Gammer Boffin\030Collect Toad-stone (total: 4)\tToads can be found in Rushock Bog, west of Overhill, beyond Hobbiton, and also in the marsh just north of Frogmorton. Gammer Boffin is in Overhill, a town nestled in the Bindbole Wood. Before you can hunt new queens for Farmer Proudfoot's hives, he sent you to Gammer Boffin to get some salve to protect you from the stings of the wild bees; however, Gammer Boffin does not have all the ingredients she needs to prepare the salve. She has asked you to collect some toad-stones for the salve.\n",
[747]="70047A82\n1\tUse Water-skin\tStanding water can be found within the caverns of Skoironk. You should collect samples of the water within the caverns for Thurindol.\n2\tSpeak with Thurindol\tThurindol can be found at a small Ranger outpost hidden in the Slag-hills. You should speak with Thurindol.\n",
[748]="7001E98F\n1\tCollect blighted ore (total: 3)\tGâthlata lies to the south-east of Mithecad. Scattered throughout the small camp of Gâthlata, several piles of ore can be found. Eirien has asked you to collect a few samples of the ore and bring it back to her.\n2\tTalk to Eirien at Mithechad\tEirien is at Mithechad, north-west of Gâthlata. You should return the samples of ore to Eirien.\n",
[749]="700658F4\n1\tFind the source of the tremor Faranil felt\030Use Odd Little Sapling\tSearch the Ettenmoors for the tremor that stirred the earth, collect it and return it to Faranil at Glân Vraig.\n2\tCollect and deliver the sapling to Faranil at Glân Vraig\tThis was unexpected. Try once more to collect the sapling. Faranil, in Glân Vraig, wants to study the trembling little sapling.\n3\tSpeak with Faranil at Glân Vraig\tHaving delivered the sapling to Faranil, you should now speak with the horticulturist to see what she may know of this little sapling.\n",
[750]="70066664\n1\tUse Odd Little Sapling\tFind a sapling described by Cinaid, rip it out of the ground, and deliver it to Cinaid at Gramsfoot.\n2\tGet the sapling out of the ground!\tIt squealed or squeaked. You heard it. Get the sapling back to Gramsfoot.\n3\tSpeak with Cinaid at Gramsfoot about your find\tYou delivered the stubborn little sapling to the Corruptor Cinaid. Time to find out what this little creature might really be.\n",
[751]="7003FFCF\n1\tSpeak with Fuirion alone\tFuirion is in Gladion's home in Dínadab. You should speak with Fuirion.\n2\tFind and reclaim Fuirion's satchel\tThe bandit encampment is west of Dínadab in northern Lamedon. You should head to the bandit encampment to find Fuirion's satchel and return it to him. NOTE: You must complete the quest \"The Letter\" to advance.\n3\tReturn the satchel to Fuirion\tFuirion is in Gladion's home in Díndab. You should bring the satchel back to Fuirion so that he may decide what to do with this dangerous information.\n",
[752]="7002FD75\n1\tTalk to the Rohirrim scout looking for assistance\tThe Rohirrim Scout was seen heading south from the estate, across the river. Cyneswith recommends speaking to the Rohirrim scout and inquiring as to what sort of aid he is seeking.\n",
[753]="7002ADAF\n1\tFind a scarf in Winter-home\030Find an acorn scattered among the trees of Winter-home\030Gather sticks from nearby bushes (total: 2)\030Gather coal near the servants' oven\tThe materials you need to replicate Virgil's snowman can be found throughout Frostbluff. In order to replicate Virgil's snowman, you will need to gather the right materials.\n2\tBuild a scarf-wearing snowman\tThe snowman-field is outside Winter-home. Now that you have gathered the necessary supplies, you should head out to the field and find a snowpile to build your snowman.\n",
[754]="70035756\n1\tCatch frightened goats (total: 3)\tTame goats from the herd can be found in the northern High Knolls near the refugees' cave. You should catch some of the frightened goats from the Byre Tor herd and lead them back to the cave. NOTE: The goats will find their way if you become separated.\n2\tLead the goats to the cave (they will find their way if you become separated)\tThe refugees are in the cave on the peak north of Byre Tor in the High Knolls. You should lead the goats you caught to the refugees' cave.\n3\tTalk to Edhild\tEdhild is in the refugees' cave in the northern High Knolls. You should speak with Edhild.\n",
[755]="70009EC4\n1\tTalk to Lieutenant Unferth\030Collect Historical Book of Rhudaur (total: 5)\tThe books and tomes Unferth desires may be carried by Orcs, Uruks, and possibly even goblins or trolls, which can be found throughout the Ettenmoors. Lieutenant Unferth has asked you to collect any books or tomes which might uncover what Angmar seeks in the Ettenmoors.\n",
[756]="700001D8\n1\tPlace reassembled vase on display table\tGlorenglir is in Rivendell, and a table nearby would be a suitable place to set the vase you have been given. Scholar Deluros has asked you to place the vase he reassembled on the table near Glorenglir, observe her reactions, then return to him.\n2\tTalk to Deluros\tScholar Deluros is in the library of Elrond's House in Rivendell. Deluros is waiting to hear if Glorenglir recognized the vase he reassembled.\n",
[757]="70057185\n1\tTalk to Léothred at the front gate of the Beorninghús\tLéothred can be found at the front gate of the Beorninghús. You should talk to Léothred.\n2\tTalk to Grimbeorn\tGrimbeorn can be found at the Beorninghús. You should talk to Grimbeorn.\n3\tTalk to Léothred\tLéothred can be found at the front gate of the Beorninghús. You should talk to Léothred.\n",
[758]="70009EC5\n1\tTalk to Lieutenant Unferth\030Collect Historical Note of Rhudaur (total: 5)\tGoblins, Orcs, and Uruks may be found throughout the Ettenmoors. Lieutenant Unferth is located within the relative safety of Ost Ringdyr. Lieutenant Unferth is concerned that Angmar's army may be searching for something terrible in the Ettenmoors, but little of the history of the region survived Rhudaur's destruction. He is looking for any shred of information that he may find.\n",
[759]="70002E5B\n1\tTalk to Arrod\tArrod is keeping watch somewhere among the Bruinen Gorges, south-east of Thorenhad, at a position where he can overlook the road. Narlinn has asked you to check on Arrod, currently scouting the Bruinen Gorges, though likely more focused on wooing the Elf-maiden Faimir.\n",
[760]="7000111E\n1\tDefeat worms in Nan Tornaeth (total: 5)\030Seek the white stone marking the correct trail\tWorms can be found in Nan Tornaeth on the path to Calenthon's camp, which can be reached by following the northward path to Ost Thondol and taking the north-west trail at the first fork. Elrohir said to look for the white marker stone at the head of the path. Elrohir suggested you defeat a number of worms on your way to speak with Calenthon, hoping you might find some clue as to the identity of the evil which has stirred them to madness.\n2\tTalk to Calenthon\tCalenthon is at his camp, which can be reached by following the northward path to Ost Thondol and taking the north-west trail at the fork. Elrohir suggested you enlist the aid of Calenthon in finding the evil which has stirred up the worms of Nan Tornaeth.\n",
[761]="70001104\n1\tTalk to Thoroniel in the North Trollshaws\tThoroniel is south of the Wovenvales, a particularly dense spider-lair in the north-western corner of the North Trollshaws. Rochwen told you to take the road eastward to the marker-stone, then strike north into the wild from there. Rochwen has asked you to aid Thoroniel, currently scouting a lair of spiders in the North Trollshaws. You should take allies with you.\n",
[762]="700572F9\n1\tFind Frethi the Explorer\tThe Secret Stone was originally found in Moria, so that is where you must begin your search for answers. You should travel to Moria and find Frethi the Explorer.\n2\tFind a clue to the origin of the Secret Stone\tMany secrets still lie hidden within the Foundations of Stone. You should search for a clue to the origin of the Secret Stone with Frethi.\n3\tEnter the 'Secret Chamber' with Frethi\tYou have discovered the door to a secret chamber in the Foundations of Stone. You should enter the 'Secret Chamber' with Frethi.\n4\tTalk to Frethi\tFrethi is investigating the Crown Chamber within the Foundations of Stone. You should talk to Frethi.\n",
[763]="7003465D\n1\tSearch the south-western woods for signs of the refugees\tThe refugees likely fled into the woods south-west of Dunfast, away from the ice-spire where Núrzum sat and terrorized the people of town. You should search for signs of the refugees in the trees.\n2\tWhistle for Cyneberg and speak with her\tCyneberg can be called by using the whistle she gave you. You should whistle for Cyneberg and show her what you found.\n3\tSearch for another sign of the refugees\tThe refugees seem to have fled further into the woods to the south of Dunfast. You should search for more signs of them.\n4\tTalk to Cyneberg\tCyneberg can be found at your side. You can use the whistle to summon her. You should speak with Cyneberg.\n5\tFind the refugees and talk to Cyneberg\030Use Whistle\tThe source of the voices can be found south of Dunfast. You should head towards the voices in the woods.\n6\tTalk to a refugee in the camp\tThe refugees can be found at their small encampment south-west of Dunfast in the Whitshaws. You should speak with a refugee of Dunfast.\n",
[764]="70062AAA\n1\tMake it to the marked spot along the road to Tharbad without running out of time\tAlla has given you five minutes to reach the spot in question along the road in view of Tharbad. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n2\tReturn to Alla in north-eastern Mossward without running out of time\tAlla is by a haystack in north-eastern Mossward. You only have five minutes for the return journey! This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n3\tTalk to Alla in north-eastern Mossward\tAlla is by a haystack in north-eastern Mossward.\n",
[765]="700174FD\n1\tShow Foreman Indrith how strong you are by flexing\tForeman Indrith is in the Wheel-house, beneath the Great Wheel. Foreman Indrith wants to make certain that you are strong enough to assist him with turning the wheel. Perhaps you should flex for him.\n2\tStep to the Wheel to aid Foreman Indrith\tForeman Indrith is in the Wheel-house, beneath the Great Wheel. Foreman Indrith has asked you to help turn the wheel.\n3\tTalk to Foreman Indrith in the Wheel-house\tForeman Indrith is in the Wheel-house, beneath the Great Wheel. After showing the foreman that you were strong enough, of which he was dubious, the two of you attempted to turn the wheel behind him. A terrible noise was heard, and the foreman looked baffled.\n",
[766]="70062130\n1\tDefeat half-orcs in Nímbarth (total: 10)\tYou should defeat half-orcs in Nímbarth to help create a distraction for Meriona and her scouts.\n2\tTalk to Meriona\tYou've created enough of a distraction for Meriona and her scouts to carry out their mission. You should talk to Meriona outside of Nímbarth.\n3\tTalk to Riderch at Stonecrop Encampment\tYou should return to Tharbad to let Riderch know that his kinsmen are safe. Stonecrop Encampment is south-west of Nímbarth.\n",
[767]="7000D916\n1\tTalk to Ponto Oats\tA burglar named Ponto is somewhere in Oatbarton, the hobbit-village on the very northern border of the Shire, almost in Evendim. You have been told to find a burglar named Ponto, somewhere in Oatbarton.\n2\tTalk to Ponto Oats and travel to Dwaling\tPonto Oats is in the village of Oatbarton. Ponto is waiting to speak with you about his plan to take care of the mean-tempered brigand in Dwaling.\n3\tTalk to Ponto Oats\tPonto Oats is in the village of Oatbarton. Ponto is waiting to speak with you about your theft of the brigand's club.\n",
[768]="7002819F\n1\tWreak revenge upon the emissary of Saruman\tThe half-orc emissary who murdered Elder Riagán and so many others among the Stag-clan can be found in the White Hand encampment you scouted in southern Trum Dreng. You should defeat this dangerous foe so that he may not harm another innocent person.\n2\tReturn to Chief Guto in Lhan Tarren\tChief Guto is in Lhan Tarren, taking the place of Elder Riagán. You should tell Guto that you have avenged his grandfather and stopped this subtle and cruel division of Isengard from continuing their destructive path.\n",
})
